This is a SESSION job: a live agent session starts it and its stdout lands in
that session. No image, no systemd unit, on purpose — scheduled, its lines would
print to nobody.

Start it from inside Claude Code with the Monitor tool (persistent: true):

    python3 -u ops/gap-watch/dd_gap_watch.py

`-u` matters: Python block-buffers stdout when it is not a terminal, and the
point is that a line reaches the session the moment it is printed.
